From 975f2c1915e9df2f87244413a4e34fb05fef4796 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 07:36:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/20] fix(deployment): stop every process group of an
 instance's session

Stopping a process instance signalled only the process group of the
instance process. Runtimes may start processes in groups of their own:
TGI's text-generation-launcher runs its router and each shard with
process_group(0). When the instance process exits, or is killed after
the grace period, such processes keep running and hold the GPUs that
the allocation is about to give to another service.

Every instance already runs in a session of its own, and processes do
not leave a session unless they call setsid. After SIGTERM and the
grace period, send SIGKILL to every process group of the session (read
from /proc on Linux) and keep doing so until neither the instance
process nor any other process of the session is left, failing after
KILL_WAIT_SECONDS as before. Without /proc only the instance process
and its own group are covered, as before.
